' 5. Take unit assessment
' Use case: Take unit assessment (Practice) · Actor: Learner
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Repository: assessment progress, mistakes
'   - Unit of work: the pass reward (XP event + total + streak) inside awardXP()
'   - Decorator: action() around the controller
'   Design choice worth a note: answers are graded on the server; the questions sent to the browser never
'   contain the answer keys.
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 05 Take unit assessment
title 5. Take unit assessment
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Learner
boundary "Web app" as Web
control "Unit controller" as Ctrl
control "Assessment service" as Svc
control "Gamification\nservice" as Gam
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB

Learner -> Web : open Unit N assessment
Web -> Ctrl : GET /api/units/:unitId/assessment
Ctrl -> Svc : getAssessment()
Svc -> Repo : unit unlocked? all lessons done?
alt not yet
  Svc --> Web : 403 + reasons
end
Svc --> Web : 15 questions **without the answers**
Learner -> Web : answer every question
Web -> Ctrl : POST /api/units/:unitId/assessment (answers)
Ctrl -> Svc : submitAssessment()
Svc -> Svc : grade on the server (pass at 80%)
Svc -> Repo : save attempt (best score kept; a pass is never lost)
Repo -> DB : UPSERT user_assessment_progress
Svc -> Repo : record answers in the mistake notebook
Svc -> Repo : record streak day
opt passed
  Svc -> Gam : reward "assessment" (100 XP, once per unit)
  group «Unit of work» awardXP()
    Gam -> Repo : XP event + XP total
  end
  Gam -> Repo : check achievements (e.g. Japanese Beginner)
end
Ctrl --> Web : score, passed, unit completed, reward
alt passed
  Web --> Learner : "Unit complete", next unit unlocks, "+XP"
else failed
  Web --> Learner : score + what to review
end
@enduml
